{"title":"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the number line between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> equal parts. The numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are marked on the line.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:Error mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Special:Upload&amp;wpDestFile=2026CayleyProblem4\" class=\"new\" title=\"File:2026CayleyProblem4\"><span class=\"mw-file-element mw-broken-media\">File:2026CayleyProblem4</span></a></span>\n</p><p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/2/7c24d29f126fbc320ed27d99b59ab2aa4291a108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N - M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c90edc3f6cea9863c70d61cfcd6c7fe26a2424fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   4.0 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\   3.5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\   3.0 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\   4.5 \\qquad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\   5.0 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"455\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> equal parts and the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/5/1a5fba937c6ab8afa92c30bc34af5abff037217f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 0 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, the distance between two consecutive ticks is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/4865cfcb1eda7283e46bbb5414b98cac7e2e69f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6}{12} = \\frac{1}{2} = 0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ticks to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ticks to the right of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/8/978ef330ea970d695e776557548499a847171516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = 0.5 \\times 2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/684f6c9b6c4f752bb3f7a79262cb1fbbf0be9fc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 0.5 \\times 9 = 4.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b592cd9c0202e4ae62c65844e4c27cca0b898ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N - M = 4.5 - 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } 3.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"233\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley\">2026 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b